 
          <p><em>A miserable little pile of secrets. But enough talk! Have at those stickers!</em> is what Dracula would say when encountering my now completely screwed up laptop. In fact, his image&mdash;including the iconic quip&mdash;is placed prominently in the middle.</p>
<p>What started with <a href="/post/2026/10/laptop-stickers-yay-or-nay/">just four stickers, mostly Emacs (Lisp) related</a> quickly spiralled out of control after the arrival of my Redbubble order. I&rsquo;m sorry, I tried neatly arranging them, I really did. But the end result is, as my wife called it, chaotic<sup id="fnref:1"><a href="#fn:1" class="footnote-ref" role="doc-noteref">1</a></sup>. But in D&amp;D, chaotic alignments can be good as well, right? Minsc is chaotic good? Sarevok can turn into being chaotic good if you treat him well in <em>Throne of Bhaal</em>? So here&rsquo;s my chaotic good laptop:</p>
<p>
<figure><a href="https://brainbaking.com/post/2026/10/what-is-a-man-laptop-stickers-part-deux/laptop.jpg" class="lbox">
		<img src="https://brainbaking.com/post/2026/10/what-is-a-man-laptop-stickers-part-deux/laptop.jpg" loading="lazy" title="The 2020 MacBook Air covered in gloriously weird stickers." data-pagefind-index-attrs="title">
	</a>
	
		<figcaption>The 2020 MacBook Air covered in gloriously weird stickers.</figcaption></figure>
</p>
<p>Now it&rsquo;s just a matter of time before a conversation is sparked. It will depend on the sticker they choose to discuss whether they&rsquo;ll become besties. While Ton chooses not to apply stickers <a href="https://www.zylstra.org/blog/2026/10/laptop-stickers-nay/">to avoid a  conversation</a> about their meaning, I am actively trying to provoke it. Dear students, if you&rsquo;re reading this: surprise me!</p>
<p>Why don&rsquo;t you try to guess which is which? I&rsquo;ll hand out a few hints for each sticker and reveal their true nature in a spoiler tag below. From the top left to the bottom right:</p>
<ol>
<li>Big black cloudy square: FSF.</li>
<li>Pixelated weirdo in long darkblue coat: an old pirate.</li>
<li>Mini round foil sticker: a certain Paw that needs to be Patrolled.</li>
<li>Big green skull: think old French adventure game.</li>
<li>What is a man: I think I already spoiled that one; but which game?</li>
<li>Next level round one: fantasy console</li>
<li>Pixelated kid dressed in green clothers holding up a sword: does this really need a hint?</li>
<li>Warning: this product may contain trace amounts of Lisp: an alien!</li>
<li>Feeling Extra Fine: a <em>fine</em> writing implement</li>
<li>A shocked skeleton: what&rsquo;s the opposite of Mario?</li>
<li>A towering purple tentacle: travel in time to find out</li>
<li>Green pixelated asparagus: just food</li>
<li>A round white <code>E</code>: the logo of an editor I&rsquo;m using right now</li>
<li>Mini round foil sticker: has a little brother called George</li>
<li>A sink overflowing: GNU Emacs is literally on it</li>
<li>We Rise At Dawn frog: what&rsquo;s inside the jar?</li>
<li>Small pixelated bug: involving grid-based tactical manoeuvring</li>
<li>An old wizard with long beard sitting on a chair: related to the green skull</li>
<li>Small pixelated bug: see 17</li>
<li>Menacing looking black bearded fellow with hat: looking for that pirate</li>
</ol>
<details class="spoiler">
  <summary>(The true meaning of the stickers)</summary>
  <ol>
<li>Big black cloudy square: The Free Software Foundation.</li>
<li>Pixelated weirdo in long darkblue coat: Guybrush Threepwood in <em>Monkey Island 2</em>.</li>
<li>Mini round foil sticker: A <em>Paw Patrol</em> sticker representing my youngest kid.</li>
<li>Big green skull: The main antagonist, Amoniak, in <em>Gobliins 2: The Prince Buffoon</em>.</li>
<li>What is a man: <em>Castlevania: Symphony of the Night</em></li>
<li>Next level round one: <em>UFO 50</em></li>
